    "statement_en": "The deflator turned positive in 2026Q2 and the price leg is more likely than not to hold through 2027Q1 (I-05); the September PMI output price index points to renewed factory-gate momentum. But the turn is concentrated upstream and coincides with the oil and metals shock (I-01). Private domestic demand has not turned (I-02): with the September PMI, new orders slipped below the expansion line on a three-month average, so fewer demand tests pass than the three of six that confirmation requires. Policy impulse is fading (I-03); exports help but do not satisfy the domestic-demand leg (I-04). Price leg roughly 65%, demand leg below even odds given the price leg: 30%.",
